        "agm_place": "Dilaksanakan Secara Elektronik",
        "agm_result": "Agenda #1: The meeting approved the 2025 Annual Report, the Board of Commissioners' Oversight Report, and the audited Consolidated Financial Statements, granting a full release of liability to the Board. It also ratified the Micro and Small Business Funding Program (PUMK) Financial Report.\nAgenda #2: Shareholders approved allocating 79% of the 2025 net profit as cash dividends totaling Rp44.47 trillion and 21% as retained earnings. The final dividend to be distributed is Rp376.95 per share, following an interim dividend paid in January 2026.\nAgenda #3: Authority was delegated to the majority Series B Shareholder and the Board of Commissioners to determine the 2026 remuneration for the Board and Directors and 2025 performance-based pay.\nAgenda #4: Shareholders approved the appointment of Public Accountant Yovita and KAP Purwanto Susanti dan Surja (Ernst & Young Global Limited) to audit the 2026 financial statements and PUMK reports.\nAgenda #5: The meeting approved the updated Recovery Plan in compliance with OJK Regulation No. 5 of 2024 and authorized the Board to execute necessary actions.\nAgenda #6: The company reported on the realization of funds used from Green Bond I Phase II 2025 and Sustainability Bond I Phase I 2025. This item was for reporting purposes only and did not require a shareholder decision.\nAgenda #7: Shareholders approved a share buyback program with a maximum value of Rp1.167 trillion and the allocation of treasury stocks for employee and management share ownership programs.\nAgenda #8: Authority was delegated to the Board of Commissioners, with approval from Series B shareholders, to approve the 2026-2030 Long-Term Work Plan (RJPP) and 2027 Annual Work Plan (RKAP).\nAgenda #9: The meeting approved amending the Articles of Association to reclassify 485,333,332 Series B shares owned by the Republic of Indonesia into Series A Dwiwarna shares.\nAgenda #10: Shareholders approved changes to the management composition, including the reappointment of Timothy Utama as Director of Operations and the confirmation of a 12-member Board of Directors and 6-member Board of Commissioners.\nAgenda #11: The Board of Directors was granted power of attorney to notarize meeting decisions and perform necessary adjustments required by authorities.\nAgenda #12: The meeting achieved a quorum with 85.5975% shareholder attendance, and the official summary of the results was submitted by the Corporate Secretary on April 30, 2026."
